{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00079",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 4.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Afternoon, doctor. They're in and comfortable, and I have the measurements ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.13,
      "end_seconds": 9.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.89,
      "end_seconds": 26.33,
      "duration_seconds": 15.44,
      "text": "Um, so... cramping pain in the lower tummy. That's why I came. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.23,
      "end_seconds": 29.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.32,
      "end_seconds": 39.81,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "Probably about a month. Yeah. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know, you know. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.13,
      "end_seconds": 44.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.52,
      "end_seconds": 60.23,
      "duration_seconds": 14.71,
      "text": "Severe, I'd say. Only passing stool, and it's not much. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I've been passing a lot of wind too, uh, for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.3,
      "end_seconds": 64.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.66,
      "end_seconds": 71.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "I'd say moderate. There was a feeling of not emptying fully, yes, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.52,
      "end_seconds": 79.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.6,
      "end_seconds": 83.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Hmm, thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.2,
      "end_seconds": 87.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any weight loss or anaemia?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.3,
      "end_seconds": 91.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "No weight loss or anaemia, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.2,
      "end_seconds": 100.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Have you had any fever, family history of bowel cancer or night-time diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.89,
      "end_seconds": 103.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.63,
      "end_seconds": 106.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.04,
      "end_seconds": 111.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Um, nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.69,
      "end_seconds": 115.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.28,
      "end_seconds": 117.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.08,
      "end_seconds": 122.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.94,
      "end_seconds": 134.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.78,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 135.33,
      "end_seconds": 139.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse 70, blood pressure 124 over 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.76,
      "end_seconds": 157.19,
      "duration_seconds": 16.43,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.12,
      "end_seconds": 161.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.98,
      "end_seconds": 165.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.78,
      "end_seconds": 171.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Pantoprazole. I take it 40 milligrams, before breakfast for my acidity."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 171.54,
      "end_seconds": 175.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 80 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.59,
      "end_seconds": 179.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.51,
      "end_seconds": 184.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "No, I left it at home. It's escitalopram, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.33,
      "end_seconds": 187.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.26,
      "end_seconds": 192.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "10 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.42,
      "end_seconds": 196.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.92,
      "end_seconds": 197.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.75,
      "end_seconds": 216.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.45,
      "end_seconds": 219.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "My mother had high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.34,
      "end_seconds": 223.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.79,
      "end_seconds": 224.65,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.41,
      "end_seconds": 245.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.99,
      "end_seconds": 252.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "Penicillin. I come out in... well, swelling of my face. Yes, dust. I get itchy eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.44,
      "end_seconds": 254.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.7,
      "end_seconds": 257.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.13,
      "end_seconds": 270.33,
      "duration_seconds": 12.2,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.21,
      "end_seconds": 273.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Yeah, that's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.75,
      "end_seconds": 280.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.39,
      "end_seconds": 291.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "I've got acid reflux. I've had anxiety for five years now. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.1,
      "end_seconds": 297.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Mm-hm. Right, so that's your known acid reflux. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.09,
      "end_seconds": 302.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.53,
      "end_seconds": 304.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.71,
      "end_seconds": 308.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.57,
      "end_seconds": 320.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Soft tummy, a bit tender on the left lower side, no masses."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.72,
      "end_seconds": 348.14,
      "duration_seconds": 21.42,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Right, here's what I'm thinking. I think we're dealing with irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis at this stage. I can't rule out coeliac disease yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.71,
      "end_seconds": 350.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.52,
      "end_seconds": 372.75,
      "duration_seconds": 21.23,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis, and we'll know more once the a stool calprotectin is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had cramping pain in the lower tummy for about a month, severe, and no night-time diarrhoea or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.86,
      "end_seconds": 375.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.35,
      "end_seconds": 391.15,
      "duration_seconds": 14.8,
      "text": "Let's get a stool calprotectin, for bowel symptoms. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Let's get blood tests, for bowel symptoms. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.22,
      "end_seconds": 412.57,
      "duration_seconds": 20.35,
      "text": "Let's use mebeverine, 135 milligrams, three times a day, for four weeks. You take it by mouth. That should help with abdominal cramps. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Regular meals and a bit more fibre, and don't rush your toilet time. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.04,
      "end_seconds": 419.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.46,
      "end_seconds": 421.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.39,
      "end_seconds": 429.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 430.89,
      "end_seconds": 431.59,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.79,
      "end_seconds": 439.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 439.96,
      "end_seconds": 444.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Sure, um, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 444.82,
      "end_seconds": 451.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 453.14,
      "end_seconds": 462.48,
      "duration_seconds": 9.34,
      "text": "So, I take the mebeverine, 135 milligrams, three times a day and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 463.64,
      "end_seconds": 466.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 466.57,
      "end_seconds": 472.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Okay, you know, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    }
  ]
}